# Application deployment automation

When changing application deployment or operational automation, read
`docs/conventions/application-deployment-automation.md`.

Keep automation proportional to the application and its operator. Put behavior
in version-controlled scripts that can be run directly; keep Rundeck or another
job runner as a thin parameter, permission, and logging layer. Prefer existing
team tools and conventions over introducing a platform stack merely because it
would suit a larger system.

For mutable actions, support a useful dry-run where practical and deliberate
non-secret debug logging. Do not use global shell tracing in scripts that can
access credentials. Test cheap behavior locally, then use the real QA
environment for integration rather than building cloud mocks by default.

Where a project already uses Ansible, run `ansible-lint` and
`ansible-playbook --syntax-check` on changed playbooks and roles as part of
that local verification.
